#What the script is doing

This script automates pulling topline measurement results into your master sheet. It works across four tabs:
	•	Brand Lift Summary
	•	Conversion Lift Summary
	•	Sales Lift Summary
	•	Visitation Summary

For each tab, it:
	1.	Looks for a row with a raw data link
	2.	Opens the linked file (or folder)
	3.	Pulls the topline / overall results
	4.	Maps those results into the correct columns
	5.	Stamps the row with a Data Extraction Date

⸻

When the script runs on a row

It only processes rows where:
	•	A raw link exists
	•	AND the Data Extraction Date is blank

It skips rows where:
	•	There’s no link
	•	OR the row has already been processed (date is filled in)

The Data Extraction Date acts as the “done” flag so nothing gets reprocessed.

⸻

What kinds of links it supports

The script can handle:
	•	Full Google Drive links
	•	Raw file IDs
	•	Folder links
	•	Folder IDs

If it’s a folder, it tries to pick the most relevant file (based on names like “topline”, “summary”, “final”, etc.).

⸻

General extraction rules
	•	Only pulls topline / overall results (not detailed cuts)
	•	Works across Docs, Slides, Sheets, and PDFs (via OCR)
	•	If something can’t be confidently found → it stays blank
	•	No guessing or filling in questionable data

⸻

Confidence values

All confidence levels are standardized to one of:
	•	80%
	•	90%
	•	95%
	•	Not Significant
	•	Not Available

⸻

Advertiser & measurement partner
	•	Advertiser
	•	Use it if it’s explicitly stated
	•	Otherwise try to infer it from the file name or content
	•	If unclear, leave blank
	•	Measurement Partner
	•	Only populate if clearly identified (e.g., Kantar, Upwave, DISQO)
	•	Otherwise leave blank

⸻

Tab-specific logic

Brand Lift Summary

Pulls:
	•	Control Response
	•	Exposed Response

And fills 5 KPIs:
	1.	Awareness / Aided Awareness
	2.	Familiarity
	3.	Favorability
	4.	Consideration
	5.	Intent / Purchase Intent

Each KPI includes:
	•	Control
	•	Treated
	•	Absolute Lift
	•	Confidence

If needed:
	•	Control = Treated - Lift
	•	Treated = Control + Lift

⸻

Conversion Lift Summary

The script doesn’t just grab conversions in order — it ranks them by funnel stage:
	•	CVR Type → most downstream (Purchase, Sign-Up, Install, etc.)
	•	CVR Type 2 → mid-funnel (Checkout, Lead, Trial)
	•	CVR Type 3 → upper funnel (Page View, Initiate Download)

For each:
	•	Lift
	•	Confidence
	•	Incremental Count
	•	CPIC

⸻

Sales Lift Summary

Maps results into:
	•	Sales Type → Total / Overall Sales
	•	Sales Type 2 → Online / eCom / Digital
	•	Sales Type 3 → In-Store

Pulls:
	•	Sales Lift
	•	Confidence (primary only)
	•	Incremental Sales
	•	IROAS

⸻

Visitation Summary

Pulls:
	•	Visit Lift %
	•	Incremental Visits
	•	CPIV

Important:
	•	Ignore anything related to Visit Lift Index

⸻

How the parsing works

The script is designed to handle messy, inconsistent formats. It:
	•	Looks at nearby text around KPIs
	•	Handles table-style data (like rows from Sheets)
	•	Works even when formatting varies across vendors

⸻

Design approach
	•	Keeps things lightweight and modular
	•	Uses shared logic across tabs, with specific rules per tab
	•	Avoids overwriting existing data
	•	Only processes what’s needed
